\f0\fs22 \cf2 The Rock Against Revival ended a little before midnight. Reluctantly, the Airborne headed for limos and hover-pad stalks, and the rest for buses, taxis and trains. Some of the Elvi were picked up in dilapidated Cadillacs, Lincolns and the occasional Arkansas Motors Grizzly. As the crowd dispersed into smaller mobs, they chorused various lines from songs they\'92d heard, the most common being 
\f1\i We can\'92t go on as Elvi with religious minds
\f0\i0 , and 
\f1\i Praise the Dawkins he\'92s the one
\f0\i0 . An enthusiastic contest broke out among factions singing preferred lines until all the mobs found themselves singing as one:
