\f3\fs24 \cf2 <!$Scr_Ps::0><$Scr_Ps::2>
\f0\fs22 Chanta arrived a little before lunch, in a reasonably presentable Cadillac the colour of the flesh of an avocado that had been left too long in the bowl. An honour guard escorted him from the kerb, between a florist\'92s trolley and a pallet of portaloo chemicals. He stepped out onto the plaza with a cap pulled low and the general bearing of a man whose head hurt, and for nearly four minutes nobody knew him at all. He liked those four minutes. He joined the barbecue queue at its proper end and studied the menu board, which said, in chalk: 
\fs20 EVERYTHING. NO SUBSTITUTIONS.\
